OVERVIEW: Convert DICOM files between transfer syntaxes and export to image
formats

Convert DICOM files to different transfer syntaxes or export pixel data to PNG,
JPEG, or TIFF.
Supports both single file and batch directory conversion.

Frames are numbered from 1 (PS3.3 Table 10-3); select one with --frame-number.
Exit codes: 0 success; 1 a file failed (a directory run exits 1 when any file
failed) or --frame and --frame-number were both given; 64 invalid arguments.

Examples:
  dicom-convert file.dcm --output output.dcm --transfer-syntax
ExplicitVRLittleEndian
  dicom-convert ct.dcm --output ct.png --apply-window --window-center 40
--window-width 400
  dicom-convert input/ --output output/ --transfer-syntax
ExplicitVRLittleEndian --recursive
  dicom-convert xray.dcm --output xray.jpg --format jpeg --quality 95
  dicom-convert cine.dcm --output frame3.png --frame-number 3

USAGE: dicom-convert [<options>] <input-path> --output <output>

ARGUMENTS:
  <input-path>            Path to DICOM file or directory

OPTIONS:
  -o, --output <output>   Output file or directory path
  --transfer-syntax <transfer-syntax>
                          Target transfer syntax: ExplicitVRLittleEndian,
                          ImplicitVRLittleEndian, ExplicitVRBigEndian, DEFLATE,
                          JPEGBaseline, JPEGExtended, JPEGLossless,
                          JPEGLosslessSV1, JPEG2000Lossy, JPEG2000Reversible,
                          JPEG2000LosslessOnly, JPEG2000Part2Lossy,
                          JPEG2000Part2Lossless, JPEG2000Part2LosslessOnly,
                          HTJ2KLossy, HTJ2KReversible, HTJ2KLosslessOnly,
                          HTJ2KRPCLLosslessOnly, JPEGLSLossless,
                          JPEGLSNearLossless, JPEGXLLossy, JPEGXLReversible,
                          JPEGXLLosslessOnly, JPEGXLRecompression, RLELossless.
                          Also a Transfer Syntax UID or a PS3.6 Table A-1
                          keyword (DeflatedExplicitVRLittleEndian,
                          HTJ2KLossless, HTJ2KLosslessRPCL, JPEG2000Lossless,
                          JPEG2000MC, JPEG2000MCLossless, JPEGBaseline8Bit,
                          JPEGExtended12Bit, JPEGXLJPEGRecompression,
                          JPEGXLLossless); every Table A-1 keyword selects its
                          Table A-1 UID. Changed: JPEG2000Lossless,
                          HTJ2KLossless and JPEGXLLossless now select .90 /
                          .201 / .110; the reversible encode into .91 / .203 /
                          .112 is JPEG2000Reversible, HTJ2KReversible,
                          JPEGXLReversible.
  --format <format>       Output format for image export: png, jpeg, tiff,
                          dicom (default: dicom) (default: dicom)
  --quality <quality>     JPEG quality (1-100, default: 90) (default: 90)
  --apply-window          Apply window/level during export
  --window-center <window-center>
                          Window center value (Window Center (0028,1050))
  --window-width <window-width>
                          Window width value (Window Width (0028,1051), at
                          least 1)
  --frame-number <frame-number>
                          Frame to export, numbered from 1 (PS3.3 Table 10-3:
                          the first Frame is Frame number 1; default 1)
  --frame <frame>         deprecated: 0-based index; use --frame-number
  --recursive             Process directories recursively
  --strip-private         Strip private tags during conversion
  --validate              Validate output after conversion
  --force                 Force parsing of files without DICM prefix
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

